-- title:
--   Shift by a normalising idele acts by right multiplication
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $O$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is an order in the sense of [`QuaternionAlgebra.IsOrder`](def/QuaternionAlgebra_Order.html#L11): it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, its $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$, and it is finitely generated over $\mathbb{Z}$. Let $n$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q},\mathrm{fin}}$ (the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$) which normalises $O$ adelically, in the sense that [`Submodule.conjByFiniteIdele O n`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L31) $=O$, i.e. the preimage under $d\mapsto d\otimes 1$ of the additive subgroup $n\cdot\mathrm{finiteAdeleBox}(O)\cdot n^{-1}$ is exactly $O$, where $\mathrm{finiteAdeleBox}(O)$ is the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes \alpha$ with $z\in O$ and $\alpha$ an integral finite adele. Put $U=\mathrm{finiteIdeleStabilizer}(O)$, the stabiliser of $\mathrm{finiteAdeleBox}(O)$ under the multiplication action of the adelic unit group, and let $\mathrm{ClassSet}(U)$ denote the double coset space of that unit group by the image of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]^{\times}$ on the left and $U$ on the right. Then for every adelic unit $x$, the shift map [`CerednikDrinfeld.classSetShift`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_ClassSetGraph.html#L22), defined on a class $c$ by choosing a representative $c.\mathrm{out}$ and forming the class of $c.\mathrm{out}\cdot n$, sends the class of $x$ to the class of $x\cdot n$.
--
--   The statement says that, for an idele normalising the order adelically, the shift of the class set $\mathbb{H}^{\times}\backslash\widehat{\mathbb{H}}^{\times}/\widehat{O}^{\times}$ defined through chosen double coset representatives is simply right multiplication by $n$, so that the shift is well defined independently of the representative. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld coset-graph constructions, where the edge orders are normalised by the relevant ideles.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CerednikDrinfeld_classSetShift_mk_of_conjByFiniteIdele_eq.lean

